// Ambiguity guard for an ERROR-SET name in a CLOSURE-LITERAL return
// annotation (`() -> !IoErr { … }`). `main` flat-imports two modules
// that each author a same-name `IoErr` and authors none itself, so the closure
// literal's `-> !IoErr` channel is a genuine collision the source cannot
// disambiguate. It emits the LOUD "type 'IoErr' is ambiguous" diagnostic and
// poisons the channel, never picking a global `findByName` last-wins author.
//
// The pre-lowering closure-shape pass (`convergeClosureShapeSets` →
// `recordClosureShape`) resolves every closure literal's return annotation
// through the source-aware `resolveType` (`resolveTypeWithBindings`), which
// routes error-set authors, so the ambiguity is detected there and reported
// regardless of `lowerLambda`. (For a `-> !Named` set that pass bails early
// after resolving, so OWN-WINS membership flows through `lowerLambda`'s own
// channel resolution — 0813 exercises that leg.) This file holds the lambda
// `-> !Named` ambiguity reported across both source-aware sites.

#import "modules/std.sx";
#import "0814-modules-same-name-error-set-lambda-ambiguous/a.sx";
#import "0814-modules-same-name-error-set-lambda-ambiguous/b.sx";

main :: () -> i32 {
    fail_io := () -> !IoErr { return; };
    return 0;
}
